{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nA rebar client installing from source reported this minor issue alongside the archived-child claim bug (b7a2-4453-3bbd-4a54). `pipx install \"<path>[agents]\"` fails when pipx selects a host uv older than 0.9.17, with an error saying pipx needs uv>=0.9.17 but the host reports 0.7.18. The failure reads like a rebar packaging problem even though it is a host pipx/uv toolchain mismatch.\n\n## Approach\nAdd a troubleshooting note to `docs/local-dev-env.md` beside the existing source-install guidance. State the uv version requirement, show `pipx install --backend pip \"<path>[agents]\"` as the clean workaround, and explicitly distinguish the host toolchain mismatch from a rebar packaging defect. No package metadata or runtime behavior changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `docs/local-dev-env.md` states that pipx installations can fail when the selected host uv is older than 0.9.17 and shows `pipx install --backend pip \"<path>[agents]\"`; verified with `grep -F -- \"--backend pip\" docs/local-dev-env.md` and `grep -F \"uv>=0.9.17\" docs/local-dev-env.md`.\n- [ ] The note explicitly identifies the failure as a host pipx/uv toolchain issue rather than a rebar packaging defect; verified by reading the rendered paragraph in context.\n- [ ] Repository lint remains green; verified with `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785555723386244001,"uuid":"a3cadab7-a9e5-4d61-9320-420ba1feca1c"}